=== PARITY (vs web RegexTester.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web source's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`; it is a pure, synchronous, local
    tool (a `RegExp` evaluation in a `useMemo`) with NO data hook, NO network, NO query, NO cache.
    The native parity binds through a local P1/S8 state holder (RegexTesterModel) that owns
    pattern + flags + testString and re-derives `evaluation` on each input change (the @Observable
    analogue of the web `useMemo` over [pattern, flags, testStr]). The view performs no HTTP — there
    is none to perform.
  Evaluation -> RegexEvaluator.evaluate is a faithful port of the web matcher, verified against
    NSRegularExpression so the indices match `m.index` exactly:
      * empty pattern OR test string  -> .idle      (web `if (!pattern || !testStr) return []`)
      * pattern/flags do not compile  -> .invalid   (web `try { new RegExp(...) } catch { [] }`;
                                                      unknown/duplicate flag -> JS SyntaxError -> nil)
      * global flag  -> collect every match left-to-right, STOP after the first empty (zero-width)
                        match (web `while (re.exec) { push; if (!m[0]) break }`)
      * non-global   -> a single match (web single `re.exec`)
    Flags map g -> global, i -> .caseInsensitive, m -> .anchorsMatchLines. Match `index` is the
    UTF-16 offset (NSRange.location == JS m.index; emoji-offset test pins it). EXECUTED unit tests
    cover \d+ global/non-global, case-insensitive, multiline anchors (with/without m), the zero-width
    break, a leading zero-width match, and the UTF-16 index.
  Composition -> ToolCard header (red `chevron.left.forwardslash.chevron.right` glyph = web lucide
    `Regex` + color "red" -> statusDanger via TSIconBox; localized title + description) · pattern
    field with a leading glyph (web `Input` + icon, prompt `\d+`) · flags menu Picker (web `Select`,
    5 options) laid out two-up on a regular width / stacked on compact (web `grid sm:grid-cols-2`)
    via ViewThatFits · test-string editor (web `Textarea` rows=3 + prompt overlay) · match-count
    badge (web `Badge` success/neutral) · match rows (web ordinal `Badge` + monospaced red `code` +
    "At Index {n}"). Regex inputs disable autocorrection (+ iOS autocapitalization) so patterns type
    cleanly. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (web "Charts/maps used: (none)").
  Shared components -> TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel/ToolCard shell), TSIconBox + TSTone (the tinted
    icon box), TSFadeIn (results reveal); the labeled inputs + the dynamic-text badge are reproduced
    as private subviews (the shared <ToolCard>/<Input>/<Select>/<Textarea>/<Badge> atoms' native
    peers are owned by other prompts, and TSBadge takes a LocalizedStringKey whereas the count/ordinal
    are runtime strings) — everything else is the P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing /
    TSRadius). No KMP `Shared` import.
  States (all render) -> the web source has FOUR evaluation branches, each reproduced with a
    #if DEBUG preview AND unit tests:
      * idle    (web early return [])      -> neutral "0 Matches" badge + a friendly "enter a
                pattern…" hint (contract: never a blank box).
      * invalid (web catch -> [])          -> neutral "0 Matches" badge + a leaf "Invalid pattern"
                notice (sanctioned leaf enhancement; the web's data semantics are unchanged — the
                badge still reads 0/neutral).
      * no-match (valid, 0 results)         -> neutral "0 Matches" badge + "No matches".
      * matches (valid, >=1)                -> success badge + the match list.
    The generic loading / stale / offline states from the prompt's checklist have NO trigger on this
    surface: it is a synchronous local tool with no async data source (no spinner), no freshness
